              "created_at": 1793596114,
              "web_search_used": false,
              "addressed_to": "",
              "display_name": "Assistant",
              "input_tokens": 143557,
              "output_tokens": 302,
              "participant_id": "builtin-assistant",
              "text": "Claude Test already has **Reasoning effort = high** saved, but its provider, **anthropic-direct**, uses CHA\u2019s native **Anthropic** integration with `claude-sonnet-4-5`.\n\n**That integration uses model-default thinking and ignores both effort and temperature.** Consequently, changing effort to High does not control Claude\u2019s thinking behavior. The provider\u2019s saved effort of `none` is **not overriding** the character\u2019s `high`\u2014neither setting controls thinking in this integration.\n\nThe two effort controls have different scopes, but neither affects native Anthropic:\n- **Characters \u2192 Claude Test \u2192 Character settings \u2192 Reasoning effort** saves the character\u2019s default.\n- The chat toolbar\u2019s **Effort** overrides it for the current session only. **Default** restores the configured effort; likewise, **Model \u2192 Default** restores the configured provider.\n\nI haven\u2019t changed anything. This is an integration limitation, not a missing High setting.",
